\section{Introduction}
% ============================================================

\subsection{Background}

Financial markets generate large amounts of structured and unstructured data every day. Stock prices, trading volume, historical price movements, technical indicators, financial news, company information, and market sentiment can all influence the movement of financial instruments. Traditional stock analysis generally requires users to collect and interpret these different sources of information manually. This makes the process time-consuming and difficult, particularly for beginner and individual investors.

Recent developments in machine learning, natural language processing, and large language models provide opportunities to build intelligent systems capable of processing financial data automatically. An AI-based stock analysis system can combine real-time market data, historical information, technical indicators, financial news, and sentiment analysis to provide data-driven analysis of stocks. The proposed system will also provide a paper trading environment where users can practice trading strategies using virtual money without risking real capital.

\subsection{Motivation}

The motivation behind this project is to develop a unified platform that combines conventional financial analysis with artificial intelligence. Existing applications often provide market charts, news, technical indicators, or trading simulation as separate features. Users may therefore need multiple platforms to perform complete stock analysis.

The proposed system aims to integrate these functionalities into a single platform. It will provide real-time stock visualization, technical analysis, financial sentiment analysis, machine learning-based prediction, AI-assisted explanations, backtesting, portfolio analysis, and paper trading. The system is intended primarily as an educational, analytical, and research platform rather than a system for guaranteed financial predictions or investment advice.

\subsection{Problem Statement}

Individual investors and students often face difficulties in collecting, processing, and interpreting the large amount of financial information required for stock analysis. Existing tools may separate market data, technical analysis, financial news, sentiment analysis, prediction models, and paper trading into different platforms.

The project aims to develop an integrated AI-based stock analysis system that collects market and financial data, performs technical and sentiment analysis, generates machine learning-based probabilistic predictions, explains the analysis using an AI assistant, and provides a risk-free paper trading environment for evaluating trading strategies.

